%S A039719 1,2,5,19,151,7571,15459161,2900549448243,71753978224278827773,
%T A039719 439096736909298481976657094853
%N A039719 Number of two-dimensional simplicial complexes on n unlabeled nodes.
%C A039719 For g in S_n, let Fix(g) be the number of labeled 2-dimensional simplicial complexes on [n] fixed by g. Then Fix(1) = A039718(n), and Fix(g) depends only on the cycle type of g. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 06 2026
%D A039719 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A039719 Vladeta Jovovic, On the number of two-dimensional simplicial complexes (in Russian), Metody i sistemy tekhnicheskoy diagnostiki, Vypusk 16, Mezhvuzovskiy zbornik nauchnykh trudov, Izdatelstvo Saratovskogo universiteta, 1991, p. 83.
%D A039719 J. R. Munkres, Simplicial Complexes and Simplicial Maps, Section 1.2 in Elements of Algebraic Topology, New York: Perseus Books Pub., pp. 7-14, 1993.
%H A039719 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/SimplicialComplex.html">Simplicial Complex</a>.
%F A039719 a(n) = (1/n!)*Sum_{cycle types c of S_n} |C_c|*Fix(c), where C_c is the conjugacy class of permutations of cycle type c, |C_c| is its size, and Fix(c) is the number of labeled 2-dimensional simplicial complexes on [n] fixed by any permutation of cycle type c. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 06 2026
%e A039719 a(6) = (3702013 + 15*67877 + 45*12101 + 15*4165 + 40*1135 + 120*197 + 40*400 + 90*185 + 90*165 + 144*28 + 120*28)/6! = 7571. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 06 2026
%K A039719 nonn,nice,hard,more,changed
